            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>The Sage Archetype is one of the three archetypes who desire nothing more but to create paradise, and to the Sage, paradise lies in understanding everything there is to understand about - well, everything!&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This attainment of knowledge is the Sages&rsquo; unique contribution to the world, and also how The Sage Archetype makes sense of the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>To the Sage, it&rsquo;s important to understand what, why, how, and what if.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Sage Archetype&rsquo;s quest for knowledge, often leads them to be the polar opposite of the Explorer archetype.Where the Explorer seeks knowledge through experience but often forgets to find out more about their internal world, the Sage seeks knowledge through understanding and often misses out in developing advanced knowledge by exploring their theories out in the real world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>True to their beliefs, Sages are almost always known for being extremely knowledgeable about pretty much anything that is interesting to them.Some Sages may never share the knowledge they attain, nor the lessons they learn whereas others may be the guru that others come to rely on for wise advice.&nbsp;</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step1-back hover prev f-left">1. Introduction</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step3 hover f-right">3. Sense of Significance</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.If we don&rsquo;t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start to become stagnant, we might develop poor confidence, and our well-being begins to deplete.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case of The Sage Archetype, they are likely to quickly attain a sense of significance - as long as they are learning something, which is reasonably easy to do.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Find The Attainment Of Significance Easy</strong></p>
                <p>Sages can easily feel significant, all they need is more knowledge and understanding to consume, and as we&rsquo;ve already alluded to, they can attain that just by living life.</p>
                <p>However, to feel as though they contribute, the Sage usually needs to be putting that knowledge to good use - for the greater good.The level of contribution they feel is entirely dependent on how many people they help, and if they get it right, it&rsquo;s unlimited.</p>
                <p><strong>Getting Out Of Their Head Is A Problem For The Sage</strong></p>
                <p>However, the Sage has a problem with getting out of their head and living life.It&rsquo;s a problem because to help people, The Sage needs to let people see them.Sages need to find a way to express themselves but find it difficult to do so.</p>
                <p>Unfortunately, many Sages find it challenging to accomplish this feat, which can lead to a lonely life and the attainment of knowledge for knowledge's sake.Such lack of connection has counter-intuitive effects on the Sages psyche. For as much as a person needs a sense of contribution and significance, they also need contact with others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Not Enough Time To Study</strong></p>
                <p>Which means that in many cases, the Sage can lead an unfulfilling and unhealthy life, if they don&rsquo;t pay attention to how they connect with others.If they succeed in connecting, and in sharing their knowledge, the potential that they have in comprehending life becomes limitless.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>However, a Sage will probably always be concerned that they won&rsquo;t have as much time to attain more knowledge if they spend it socializing and then will subsequently choose to spend their time reading or researching instead - forgetting that they can learn from their experiences too - all of them. Not just the ones they focus on.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step2-back hover f-left">2. Unique Contribution</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step4 hover f-right">4. Personality Traits</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p>Dedicated to understanding the world around them the Sage seeks out and consumes knowledge and wisdom like no other archetype, and they don&rsquo;t even need a reason to absorb this knowledge - they like to learn for the sake of learning.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Many Sages will specialize in a particular field of knowledge, usually because it's where their interests lie and also because it&rsquo;s just not possible to know everything about everything.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>More often than not though, you&rsquo;ll find a Sage seeking out philosophical truths about who we are, where we came from and where we are heading.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Positive People</strong></p>
                <p>Sages are also generally very positive people, even if they have had a difficult life.This optimism is because they believe that everything they experience in life is a lesson, and an opportunity to grow and learn.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Overthinkers</strong></p>
                <p>Being labeled as being &lsquo;deep&rsquo; or an &lsquo;overthinker&rsquo; at some point in a Sage's life is hardly surprising and very close to the truth since it&rsquo;s possible that a Sage can get lost in the depths of their knowledge and may have earned the title of being an over-thinker from time to time.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Self-Aware</strong></p>
                <p>Often what people don&rsquo;t realize is that Sages have strong intuition and self-awareness.They don&rsquo;t need to be told to become more self-reflective - they do it all the time naturally.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Curious</strong></p>
                <p>Sages are also naturally curious about pretty much anything that captures their interest, and it doesn&rsquo;t stop when they have completed their formal studies.A Sage cannot enjoy life without learning something about it.They have to know the truth behind everything.</p>
                <p><strong>Truth Seekers</strong></p>
                <p>Sages&rsquo; does not suffer fools gladly, nor do they appreciate lies and manipulation.So much so that a Sage will either remove themselves away from the situation (no matter who you are to them) or they will call you out on your behavior in a way that will make you face up to your misdemeanors.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If you have lied to a Sage, they may take the high road and forgive you, but they won&rsquo;t forget the line that you have crossed.If you are close to a Sage, be honest with them, even if you have to say things that hurt they&rsquo;ll respect you more for doing so for they have huge respect for the truth and high disregard for lies.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Sages can be Both a Blessing and an Annoyance to those around them. </strong></p>
                <p>Because of their knowledge, Sages efficiently help people and usually help many with their sound advice.But other times, when they are generally just hanging out with their friends and family, Sages can become bored because they are not learning something.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Or they may keep dropping facts and advice at a time when everyone is trying to have some fun, which means that sometimes the Sage can bore people.Sages can also unwittingly oppress others because they are aware that a Sage will have some advanced knowledge that will make their knowledge seem inferior.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sages need to learn to let go and have more fun, to live in the moment and enjoy the people around them, but it is tough for a Sage to do because they often don&rsquo;t see the point in such frivolity especially since to the Sage fun lies in the attainment of knowledge!</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even from Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side.Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it&rsquo;s discussed in great detail in our Premium Archetype Reports.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Here at Individuologist.com we realize that there is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don&rsquo;t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.It&rsquo;s this hidden aspect that can bring about great reward if we were to focus our attention on it. It&rsquo;s also crucial for helping each different archetype overcome their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Before we get started, it&rsquo;s important to acknowledge that there&rsquo;s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too and the process of individuation can help us to uncover these hidden aspects of our &lsquo;self&rsquo; too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these &lsquo;hidden&rsquo; aspects of our &lsquo;self,&rsquo; we begin to learn about what is really driving us.We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don&rsquo;t do the things that we want to do, or should do).This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires or reach our fullest potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>A Vibrant Inner World</strong></p>
                <p>The Sage often has many hidden inner thoughts, one of the issues with the Sage is that they often live in their inner world more than they do the external world.And so, the Sages secret world is usually vibrant, exciting and full of secrets.</p>
                <p>However, there will be some thoughts that a Sage has that even they might deny - perhaps because they don&rsquo;t know how to deal with them, ideas such as:</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Often Don&rsquo;t Know How To Connect With Others</strong></p>
                <p>Sages don&rsquo;t find superficial living easy at all.But they can often mistake passing time and having fun as superficial living even when it could also be considered spending quality time with those you love.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Because of this reason, Sages often feel confused and slightly disconnected by society. They don&rsquo;t usually know how to go with the flow (even if they understand the principle of it) and typically feel distant and uncomfortable in social settings.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Maybe this is because most Sages might view hanging around with others as a waste of valuable time.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Sage could realize that their external world will add to their understanding of the world and improve their knowledge and wisdom tenfold, then they might be more inclined to give themselves permission to take some time off and enjoy the company of others!</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Often Ignore Their Health Needs</strong></p>
                <p>Sages know how to adapt and are usually confident learners.Which means that they know how to learn more about what they need to do for their physical health too.</p>
                <p>But, unless it&rsquo;s a topic of interest for the Sage, they won&rsquo;t apply attention there until it&rsquo;s too late.You see, Sages only focus on learning whatever it is that they are interested in and if health is boring to them, then they don&rsquo;t learn about it.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sages often live isolated and quiet lives which are often disconnected from the physical realm, and so they are unfortunately detached from their physical body too.And because of this tendency, you can be sure that Sages probably do need to put their attention toward their health.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sages probably don&rsquo;t want to learn about their health because it is another distraction away from their pursuit of knowledge.What they forget though is that without health we are nothing!</p>
                <p><strong>They Don&rsquo;t Always Know How to Have Fun</strong></p>
                <p>Sages might want to have fun, and they might want to connect with others, but they also might not know how to go about it, and so they often stay in the comfort zone of their internal world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Even if they know it doesn&rsquo;t make them truly happy, they feel safer that way. Some Sages might never even admit this to themselves.</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Constantly weigh Up The Compromise Between Time Spent On Gaining Knowledge Versus Time Spent On Everything Else</strong></p>
                <p>One of the most significant internal conflicts that a Sage experiences, is that every time they do anything that doesn't involve gaining knowledge they will see that as a waste of their time.There&rsquo;s too much to learn in one life, and so they can become a little too obsessed in their mission.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Attaining balance and an appreciation of all things is a challenge for the Sage.</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Can Be Afraid Of The World</strong></p>
                <p>Even though Sages are fiercely seeking knowledge and would say that they wouldn&rsquo;t stop at anything to glean some information.The fact remains that most Sages are secretly afraid of stepping out into the world which prevents them from expressing their knowledge and connecting with others through their knowledge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It prevents them from seeing all sides of an issue and being able to connect the dots to find a solution.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>So, they unconsciously (or even consciously) find a distraction from having to go out into the world through their pursuit of knowledge.</p>
