            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">
                <p><strong>Sages Are Self Reflective</strong></p>
                <p>Sages are very self-aware, they often reflect on their experiences in life and glean way more information from those experiences than most other archetypes will.  They regularly check in with themselves, correcting their patterns and behaviors (that they are aware of) so that they are more aligned with how they would like to present themselves.</p>
                <p>Which means that when they read their greatest challenges detailed below, to a certain extent, they already know and understand the value of the things we suggest.  And considering that Sages are so self-reflective, they have no excuse for not taking action.</p>
                <p>Perhaps now is the time to start doing what you know you need to do, dear Sage.</p>
                <p><strong>Kind Hearted</strong></p>
                <p>While it is true that knowledge is power, Sages generally don’t seek power.  They seek to make the world better for everybody who lives on it.</p>
                <p>They come from a place of purity and of only wanting to know what is true and they do so, not just for their satisfaction but also so that they can help others too.</p>
                <p>It’s just that they need to learn to take action so that they can help the masses!</p>
                <p><strong>Intuitive</strong></p>
                <p>Sages will often check in with their intuition - it’s usually how they can perceive right from wrong.  Their sense of intuition is well-honed because it’s how they discern between facts when they are gaining knowledge and wisdom.</p>
                <p>They come from a good place and will, in most situations discount something if their intuition tells them too.</p>
                <p><strong>Wise</strong></p>
                <p>It’s all good and well-attaining knowledge, and even sharing it, but if it is not utilized wisely, then grave problems can arise.</p>
                <p>Fortunately, because the Sage is disciplined in their pursuit of knowledge, and because they are incredibly intuitive and kind natured, knowledge is in the right hands. Plus, they intend to help others. It’s hardly surprising to learn that the Sage is usually incredibly wise too.</p>
                <p>Which means when you get advice from a Sage, and it resonates with you, then you know it's credible and worth taking notice of.</p>
                
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Sages Live In Their Inner World Too Much</strong></p>
                <p>Sages tend to live in their head. They are often introverted and at ease in their own company which compounds the problem of living too much in their head further.</p>
                <p>The problem is, living an insulated life doesn’t allow the Sage to find a healthy balance in their life, nor does it assist them in their plan for creating paradise - because they end up hoarding the knowledge and not sharing it with others. </p>
                <p>It’s the act of sharing knowledge that opens up incredible opportunities for the sharer and the receiver.  Sages need to build a life that reminds them to do this and pushes them to take action out in the real world because that’s where they’ll make the most significant difference.</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Frequently Compromise Their Health</strong></p>
                <p>Sages tend to forget about all physical things because they live in their head.  And so, discipline and routine are always a challenge for Sages.  They also often lead an inactive lifestyle because of their fascination with studying over everything else, which compromises their health.</p>
                <p>It’s crucial for a Sage to discipline themselves so that they prioritize their health.</p>
                <p><strong>Sages Are Sometimes Too Opinionated</strong></p>
                <p>Sages are awkward around others most of the time.  Sure, they may have developed social skills, but they won’t feel as comfortable as others around them in a social setting.</p>
                <p>They also live a very one-dimensional life where they spend most of their time researching and studying, so when they are around others, they can sometimes be a little too deep and focused on what they’ve been learning about. Furthermore, given their vast knowledge, they can also be quite opinionated at times.</p>
                <p>This profound perspective can cause the Sage to find it even more difficult to socialize because they don’t have anything to say that is interesting to others and if they do, they’ll come across as too opinionated.</p>
                <p>Which is why the Sage will benefit from pushing themselves to join a club so that they can bring more physical diversity into their life which will eventually resolve the awkwardness they feel.</p>
