            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">
                <p>The greatest challenge for a Sage essentially lies in learning how to attain balance.A balance between;</p>
                <ul>
                <li>Attaining knowledge and appreciating the wonders of life.</li>
                <li>Attaining knowledge and taking action.</li>
                <li>Attaining the knowledge they desire, versus the knowledge they need.Such as learning how to take better care of their health and well being.&nbsp;</li>
                </ul>
                <p>So, in other words, Sages need to learn how to attain a balance between living in their internal world and connecting with their physical world.</p>
                <p><strong>The Sage Is The Opposite To The Explorer</strong></p>
                <p>The Explorer wants to explore the world through the act of doing but limits his or her experience because they never really focus on internalizing their experiences and aligning them with their inner world. Whereas the Sage is the Explorers total opposite, they explore the world internally, never fully learning how to integrate their inner world with the external world and thus only received one half of the experience.Both want to attain understanding yet only receive half of what they could potentially know or experience.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>So Much To Give To The World</strong></p>
                <p>The Sage has so much to give to the world, and so much that they could glean from the world if only they would start to step into it more often and the world has so much to gain from a Sage.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s just so unfortunate that most of the world doesn&rsquo;t know that the Sage is even there - even those close to the Sage might not truly understand the level of their knowledge and ability to help others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Sage could learn to explore the world a little more and take more action, then incredible things will happen.The Sages knowledge will increase tenfold, they&rsquo;ll learn from others, they&rsquo;ll glean more insight from the experiences of others, and in turn, they&rsquo;ll change the lives of others for the better.They&rsquo;ll develop their interests further into areas that the Sage didn&rsquo;t even know existed and they&rsquo;ll inspire and lead many into a better world - paradise even.And they would have done so by using knowledge to their advantage.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Don&rsquo;t Often Reach Their Full Potential</strong></p>
                <p>Unfortunately, though, most Sages live a quiet life, and only develop one facet of their capacity of knowledge and also remain fearful of exploring the external world - even though pushing out into the external world is part of the solution to finding the paradise the Sage yearns for.</p>
                <p><strong>How The Sage Archetype Can Master Their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>To overcome their greatest challenge the Sage needs to look at how they live their life and pay attention to what area&rsquo;s need more balance - then they need to take action toward attaining balance.</p>
                <p><strong>Seek Balance</strong></p>
                <p>If a Sage finds it difficult to attain such balance, they could implement some regular routines and structure to encourage them to put their attention to important things such as health, exercise, connection, and mindfulness.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Taking time out to consciously prepare a healthy meal will be hard for most Sages. But if they can recognize that sometimes our minds need time to assimilate the knowledge received to make the most of it it will help the Sage appreciate the opportunity to take a break from their studies.</p>
                <p>In the same vein, it wouldn&rsquo;t hurt a Sage to join a social club, such as a walking club or some other sports where they can combine exercise and socialize at the same time.Even if they only did this once per week, it would be a good step in the right direction for finding balance and getting out of their mind.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Teach What You Know</strong></p>
                <p>Another excellent way for a Sage to start to find their feet out in the real world is to begin teaching what they know, either through a blog, a video channel, a book or information products.This way they will start to open the doors to allow the opportunity for connection in a purposeful way and in a way that will make sense to them - through the exchange of knowledge!&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s crucial that the Sage learns how to connect with others and makes an effort to live in the real world fully at least 50% of their waking time.If they do so, they will develop a whole new level of knowledge that they didn&rsquo;t even realize was available to them.The rewards that the Sage will reap from this is high.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>The Sage Has All The Resources They Need</strong></p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s also useful that the Sage has all of the resources they need to learn how to overcome their fears of connecting.They are the experts at research, so it shouldn&rsquo;t take them too much time to find resources that will help more introverted people learn how to interact socially in a way that is comfortable for them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sages you really have no excuse for not taking action and attaining a healthy balance between life and knowledge.Since they have all the resources, need and out of all of the archetypes Sages are the most equipped to make this transition!&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Shadow work, in particular, is a great resource that will help you discover more about your inner self and how you can rise to your challenge, you can learn more about this in the Premium Archetype Reports.</p>
